92186045417] [17592186575552 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $A=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b,c\\in R\\}.$    \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is closed under matrix addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575552 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "63775110-b76b-5425-a979-1d472435c3ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575552 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If ${A}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1} & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & {b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ are two matrices from $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & {b}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1} & 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & {b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is not a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is  *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is an element of $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =k\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2a & 2b \\\\ 2c & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is  *not* closed under scalar  multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $A$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575644 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186575660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575644 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2f479215-92de-59bc-a9f7-99164bc800e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575644 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575658 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186575680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575658 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "63ba8bbb-db34-560b-835a-80c6cbe5aee6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575658 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575660 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "682539ca-dd28-5486-a289-41f166f6fb31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575660 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186575552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575679 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186575644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575679 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b5b4ede0-23d1-5e23-9ac1-9e7f542f0119" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575679 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186329725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575680 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186575679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575680 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bb14753a-b718-5bb4-8590-d7cdea5611b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575680 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125157 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
